column2:
Gilgameš — where are you wandering?
a+17	The life you keep hunting you will not find.
a+18	When the gods created mankind,
a+19	death they set aside for mankind;
a+20	life they kept fast in their own hands.
a+21	You, Gilgameš — let your belly be full;
a+22	keep making holiday, day and night;
a+23	every single day make a feast of gladness;
a+24	day and night, dance and play.
a+25	Let your clothing be clean and bright;
a+26	let your head be washed; be bathed in water.
a+27	Gaze at the little one holding your hand;
a+28	let a wife delight, again and again, in your lap.
a+29	Such is the destiny [of mortal men(?)] —
a+30	that the one who lives [may live his share(?).]
